    {
     "slug": "seattle-olympic-national-park",
     "number": 1,
     "title": "Seattle & Olympic National Park",
     "text": "Day one of the bikepacking adventure.  We took a ferry from Seattle across Puget Sound to the peninsula and out to Mount Olympus National Park.   One night camped next to Puget Sound, one night at Lake Crescent.  \n\nLeaving Lake Crescent, we had our first experience riding single track through the beautiful temperate rainforests of the Pacific North-West where tragedy struck.  Ross's pedal hit a rock and brought his bike to a sudden stop while he continued to soar, over the handlebars and directly into the ground.  He suffered a critical strike to his shoulder, snapping his collar bone in twain.  Thus altering our plans.  \n\nThe rescue operation took us the rest of the day as we walked out of the forest and went knocking on doors for help.  A kind local whisked him away to the nearest hospital for an assessment while I doubled back to retrieve my bike and finished the trail to reunite with him.  From there we bussed back to Poulsbo and took refuge in a motel.  \n\nThe following day, Ross' cousins traveled from Portland to collect him and take him under their care.  The remainder of our three month bikepacking adventure was now mine to do solo.",
