    {
     "slug": "north-bend",
     "number": 3,
     "title": "North Bend",
     "text": "Riding from Seattle to North Bend was a treat.  Campuses set in forests.  Bridges hopping from island to island.  Tree lined trails.  Also highways.  I learned a lesson about just letting RideWithGPS curate your journey.  I probably should have trusted my senses better and not just followed it blindly.  It took me down into a valley and up a near vertical climb, carrying my bike for parts.  It spat me out, sweaty and covered in debris at some kind of sterile golf village that looked like it was out of Edward Scissorhands.\n\nAnyway, I made it to North Bend and stayed with a kind family who let me sleep in their treehouse for a couple of nights.  North Bend is where a lot of Twin Peaks was filmed, in particular the scenes in the opening sequence and the diner.  Wholesome vibes, I can see why Agent Cooper fell in love with the place.  I stayed two nights here, spending a day just exploring the town, swimming in the river and washing my clothes.  Good times.\n",
